# Line endings are pinned, not left to each machine's git default.
#
# base-config-provenance regenerates spec/config/base/*.json and compares them
# byte-for-byte against the committed set, so a CRLF checkout fails verification
# on content that is not wrong — only its line endings are. git's default on
# Windows is core.autocrlf=true, which is exactly that checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
